.git
.github
output.log
*.log
# logs/ held 2.3 GB across 249 files by 2026-08-10 and GROWS every run; the
# bare `*.log` above matches only root-level files (the same semantics trap
# documented for *.zip below), so the whole tree was uploaded with EVERY stage
# build — measured live: "transferring context: 2.38GB 19.3s" (needed content
# is ~86 MB). Never COPY'd by any Dockerfile → zero cache impact.
logs/
**/archive/
README.md
AGENTS.md
CHANGELOG.md
.gitignore
.dockerignore
docs
linux/webserver
out/
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip
# windows/downloads is consumed ONLY by Dockerfile.nvidia, which build.ps1 builds with
# its own `windows` context (this root .dockerignore does not apply there; see
# windows/.dockerignore). Excluding the whole dir here keeps the ~2 GB EULA-gated
# TensorRT zip (plus any locally parked CUDA/cuDNN downloads) out of the ROOT context
# that every other docker build in the chain uploads (~9 per full run, classic builder
# = full context upload each). NB: a bare `*.zip` above matches only root-LEVEL zips
# (Docker pattern semantics), so this explicit dir exclusion is load-bearing.
windows/downloads/
*.swp
*.swo
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
**/node_modules/
.cache/
*.so
*.o
*.a
**/target/
**/build/
!linux/scripts/03-media/build/
!linux/scripts/03-media/build/onnxruntime/build/
**/dist/
.venv/
venv/
*.whl
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

sphinx-kataglyphis-theme/
*.vs
.vs/
*.pdb
*.exp
*.ilk

# Windows CI/template scaffolding — not consumed by any Windows Dockerfile
windows/scripts/rust/
windows/scripts/python/
windows/scripts/certificates/

# DocumANTation submodule (~9 MB): built standalone from its own Dockerfile,
# never COPY'd by any chain Dockerfile — keep it out of every root context
# upload (~9 per full classic run).
external/
